ally you can remix you can  loop you can do all sorts of things and  you can actually do it with any music  that you put on here  it's pretty good we can work with that  but how bold of kanye to create this  thing and give you the album and say  here you play with it you do whatever  you want so before i even got the stem  player yeah that's what i did i made my  own version of the album  the album cover i made  uses a picture taken by frankie vergara  go check him out on instagram or twitter  it's a picture taken of soldier field of  that final listening party and i think  it's a really cool shot i mean damn look  at this not only did i create my own  cover but i cut out some songs too  my version of the track list kind of  reflects the first listening party i  sequence this in a way that the tracks  flow into one another and there's a  broad narrative  [Music]  it all structure to life  i'm biased but i think my version flows  really well and if you want to check it  out i've got it on apple music and  spotify unfortunately even the version  on spotify isn't going to sound like  this because i had to make my own edits  to get it on a cd it is just too long so  for anybody watching this who didn't  like the album keep my spirit alive come  to life and 24. just listen to those  three tracks in a row and tell me what  you think  of course after i make my version he  puts out a deluxe  like we needed deluxe the trend of  deluxe albums is  it's frustrating for me it's essentially  a re-release of the album to give more  streams and they put three or four songs  on the end what kanye did is basically  that he made the album longer but he  also gave us a new sequence and the new  sequence is pretty bizarre i think a lot  of people would agree with that but he  also gave us some really good tracks  [Music]  never abandon your family if you  attended at least the first listening  party i know that track was there and  that was one of the most moving on the  album at the ti